# Project operating rules

Before substantial work, read `AI/GAME_DESIGN.md`, `AI/ROADMAP.md`, `AI/PROGRESS.md`, and `AI/DECISIONS.md`. When classifying remaining tests after Agent-first verification, also use `AI/PLAYTEST_BACKLOG.md`.

1. Understand the current game vision before implementing features. `AI/GAME_DESIGN.md` is the authoritative **active design bible**. It already contains approved director decisions. Preserve those decisions. Leave unresolved portions unresolved unless directors explicitly decide them. Do not independently alter game design.
2. Determine the current roadmap phase from `AI/ROADMAP.md`. Phases are dependency order, not an excuse to skip ahead.
3. Preserve established architectural and game-design decisions in `AI/DECISIONS.md` and `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`.
4. Do not silently change the game’s design.
5. Do not implement unrelated future features or major later-phase gameplay just because it is on the roadmap.
6. Keep server-authoritative gameplay logic on the server (`ServerScriptService` / `Services`).
7. Never trust the Roblox client for authoritative decisions.
8. Keep systems modular. Avoid monolithic scripts. Thin bootstraps only.
9. Use Script Sync for source-controlled Luau. Disk `StarterPlayerScripts/` maps to Studio `StarterPlayer.StarterPlayerScripts`.
10. Use Roblox Studio MCP for live DataModel work, inspection, GUI instances, and Studio Play / Local Server **development verification**. Do not put GUI instances in the filesystem. Studio sessions are **not** the project’s first real playtest (published Roblox server; see `AI/GAME_DESIGN.md`).
11. Inspect and verify the implementation before declaring completion. Follow **Agent-first verification** (rule 28).
12. Check Roblox Studio errors/output when appropriate.
13. Diagnose and correct your own implementation errors.
14. Never mark a task complete merely because code was written. Verify first. Agent verification is **not** Director acceptance.
15. After verified substantial work, update `AI/PROGRESS.md`.
16. Append meaningful completed changes to `AI/CHANGELOG.md`.
17. Record significant new architectural decisions in `AI/DECISIONS.md`.
18. Never modify `AI/GAME_DESIGN.md` to make implementation easier or to retroactively justify a coding choice. Change it only when the user explicitly requests a design change.
19. If design docs do not answer an important product question, ask the user instead of inventing a major decision.
20. **Coherent GUI-first prototype UI.** Before creating or substantially modifying GUI, inspect the live Studio GUI and current screen usage. New systems must join the existing interface as one evolving strategy-game UI, not isolated debug windows. Prototype visuals need not be final polish (**ugly is acceptable; confusing is not**), but must be readable, logically placed, and easy to test. When the interactive map/world exists, it gets primary central screen space; supporting info and actions use side panels, overlays, or other placements that do not unnecessarily block the map. Avoid Roblox CoreGui/topbar/chat overlap and unintentional project-GUI overlap. Use proper layout/container behavior for dynamic content. Important actions, state changes, requests, and notifications must be obvious enough for manual testing. If a system needs more space, reorganize the prototype coherently rather than stacking panels arbitrarily. Keep consistent spacing, section hierarchy, button conventions, and prototype styling where practical. Verify usability in Studio Play mode; Edit-mode appearance alone is insufficient. Functional consistency beats decorative polish. Do not imitate another game’s copyrighted visual assets or exact UI; aim for an original grand-strategy feel, not a CK3 clone. This is a standing implementation rule, not authorization for a full UI redesign.
21. **Admin / testing.** Kohl's Admin is command UI only, not gameplay authority. Game-state testing goes through `AdminBridge` into existing services. Do not scatter Kohl requires through gameplay services. Do not add client remotes for admin mutations. When implementing a new authoritative system, consider Admin Bridge hooks after its own APIs exist; do not invent deferred gameplay as fake admin commands. Kohl ranks below SuperAdmin do not grant GameTester access; the central server gate allows authorized UserIds or trusted effective SuperAdmin+ (Director ruling, 2026-10-10). Global admin inspection may remain even when player UI is filtered. Convenient in-game copy/reuse of reusable IDs is a later pre-playtest admin UX requirement, not current work.
22. **Player-relevant information.** Ordinary player-facing UI must not automatically display global server state. Filter to the player, their ruler, their greater realm, things they interact with, or information designed as public. Admin/debug is exempt. `PlayerRelevantView` is a view helper, not gameplay authority.
23. **Terminology.** Territory = land/province. Title = political rank (Lord/Duke/King/Emperor). Do not interchange them.
24. **Pre-playtest usability.** Player/map orientation, coherent layout, and admin copy/reuse UX are required before the first published playtest. Do not implement them unless the Director authorizes it. Do not treat them as optional decoration on the roadmap.
25. **Economy / Resources V0.1** is **IMPLEMENTED — DIRECTOR-VERIFIED — DIRECTOR-ACCEPTED** (V0.1 Gold foundation only). Do not treat this as a complete economy. Do not implement buildings, development, taxation, trade, or delegated greater-realm permissions unless the Director authorizes it. Preserve Gold / Prestige / Influence as distinct match resources. Do not introduce Credits as a Gold replacement. Do not retrofit delegation into accepted V0.1 systems. Future Gold spends must go through `EconomyService`, not direct balance mutation. Kohl GameTester target tokens use `adminOwnerToken` / `adminRulerToken` (raw parse; suggestions are not authority). A landless liege with surviving subjects is an unresolved hierarchy/title case; do not modify accepted Hierarchy, Territory, Title, Diplomacy, or Warfare to “fix” it unless the Director designs it.
26. **Military / Armies V0.1** is **IMPLEMENTED — DIRECTOR-VERIFIED — DIRECTOR-ACCEPTED** (ordinary V0.1 scope only; 18 Director PASSes in `AI/PROGRESS.md`; not a complete military game; not V0.2). Eight MIL-MP overlay/race cases remain **DEFERRED ≠ PASS** in `AI/PLAYTEST_BACKLOG.md` and do not block V0.x development; Troop duplication, dropped outcomes, double resolution, stuck CONTESTED, or equivalent authoritative corruption found later is a real defect. Do not expand into V0.2. Same-target: at most one active war per territory (10s post-war cooldown). Commitment actors: two war roots, personal Troops. Interaction = server-accepted commitment intent. Decision window **40s** (auto-lock latest accepted if interacted); hard timeout **55s** (nonresponsive attacker cancel / defender 0). Ready/dual-Ready remains an immediate path. Cancel before mechanical resolution unwinds Troops with zero casualties. Battle is mechanically final at dual-lock; 5s is presentation. Admin `resolvewar` after mechanical resolution is rejected. Hidden state: server/admin/debug only. Future Gold spends for Troops go through `EconomyService.TrySpend`. Agent-first verification (rule 28) still applies to later work. Do not mark Director-verified/accepted from agent tests. Over-Available TextBox last-valid-intermediate auto-submit is Director-accepted as-is for V0.1.
27. **Configurable keybinds** are a **future public-product** requirement (Settings / Controls; logical actions, not hardcoded physical keys). The future UI shell already requires centralized unassigned bindings. Do **not** implement Settings/Controls, remapping, persistence, or new keybinds unless the Director authorizes it. The first published playtest may use temporary/default binds; remapping is **not** automatically a first-playtest requirement. Do not over-engineer the current prototype; avoid new private per-controller physical-key GUI contracts.
28. **Agent-first verification (project-wide).** The Director is not the first-line tester for behavior the agent can reasonably verify. For every future system, feature, bugfix, refactor, integration, or implementation pass: (1) Verify as far as the environment allows **before** asking the Director to test (static inspection, Studio Play Solo, Local Server/multiplayer when available, server test hooks, flag-gated diagnostic logs, Output, debug snapshots, server-only debug invokes, AdminBridge inspect, seeded/deterministic RNG where randomness would block verification, malformed-request tests, authority/security inspection, lifecycle transitions, regressions against accepted systems). (2) Hidden-from-player information is **not** hidden from testing; provide **server-only / admin / debug** observability. Do **not** put private state on ordinary player remotes or production UI to make testing easier. (3) Temporary diagnostics must be server-only where appropriate, removable or disableable, non-authoritative, and not a client leak. (4) Verify invariants yourself when practical. (5) Director testing should focus on player-visible behavior, simple multiplayer interaction, end-to-end flows, UX, acceptance-critical integration, feel, and **final acceptance**. Cumbersome multiplayer/emergent cases may be classified under rule 29 instead of blocking V0.x progress. (6) When requesting Director testing, distinguish **AGENT-VERIFIED**, **DIRECTOR VERIFICATION REQUIRED**, **DEFERRED — NON-BLOCKING — V0.5 PLAYTEST VERIFICATION BACKLOG**, and **NOT TESTABLE IN CURRENT ENVIRONMENT** (with reason). (7) Agent verification ≠ Director acceptance. Never mark **DIRECTOR-VERIFIED** or **DIRECTOR-ACCEPTED** because agent tests passed. Never rewrite “not tested” or “deferred” into PASS. (8) Do not fake verification; report limitations instead of claiming PASS. Do not move Agent-testable cases into the human playtest backlog merely for convenience.
29. **Deferred multiplayer verification (project-wide).** Multi-client, emergent multiplayer, disconnect, race-condition, multi-ruler coordination, and similarly cumbersome Director manual tests do **not** automatically block V0.x development progress when: Agent-first verification has reasonably passed; core authoritative state/invariants are reasonably verified; the ordinary gameplay loop functions; no known critical defect remains; and remaining uncertainty is primarily multiplayer/emergent/manual. **Deferred does not mean PASS. Deferred means non-blocking until the appropriate testing stage.** Record those cases in `AI/PLAYTEST_BACKLOG.md` as **DEFERRED — NON-BLOCKING — V0.5 PLAYTEST VERIFICATION BACKLOG**. A deferred case becomes **blocking** again if Agent verification finds a concrete defect; the behavior threatens authoritative server state; it is a security/exploit risk; it risks duplication/loss/corruption of important state; it prevents the ordinary gameplay loop from functioning; or the Director explicitly promotes it back to blocking. Do not defer known serious integrity/security defects to preserve speed. Workflow: (1) Agent verifies as much as practical; (2) genuine low-level defects are fixed before handoff; (3) Director manually verifies meaningful player-facing/simple acceptance cases; (4) cumbersome multiplayer/emergent cases may be deferred to V0.5 if non-blocking; (5) deferred cases remain documented; (6) V0.5 playtest feedback is compared against the backlog. Product-direction milestones (not a feature-count claim): V0.1–V0.4 build/integrate core systems (ugly OK, confusing is not); around V0.5 first serious playtesting; V0.5–V0.9 iterate from feedback; V1.0 release target with stronger onboarding/polish. Pacing principle: **the timer should pressure indecision, not punish normal thinking.**
30. **Communications V0.x** is **PRE-V0.5 REQUIRED — IMPLEMENTED — PARTIALLY AGENT-VERIFIED — NOT DIRECTOR-ACCEPTED** (recommendation B replacement authorized 2026-10-09). Ordinary paths: Diplomatic (retired name General; sender realm-graph distance ≤ 2; asymmetric delivery is desired); Council (ruler + direct subjects only); Allies (per distinct Alliance; no NAP; no subject inheritance); Direct (1:1; current adjacency between the two rulers’ directly/personally owned territories, never root graph distance; relationship-independent including same-root; loss of border immediately cuts send access). Admin/Observer is separate (context metadata + mute). Use TextChatService direction; Roblox filtering; no keyword/number censorship of voluntary speech. The implementation authorization supersedes the prior design-only prohibition; preserve native filtering/privacy, frozen scope and deferred announcements. Do not start Phase 2 or Military V0.2 from Communications work. Canonical: `AI/GAME_DESIGN.md`.

31. **Director-authorized GUI / UX sprint (2026-10-09):** the explicit broad presentation/navigation authorization supersedes older fixed-region/no-shell restrictions for this sprint. Centralized on-screen Map/system navigation and responsive drawers are implemented by StrategyPresentationController; existing gameplay/content controllers retain contracts. No key assignments, Settings/remapping, core rules or authority changes. See AI/GUI_UX_SPRINT.md; agent verification is not Director visual or gameplay acceptance.
